ARCH: 0.4
SYS: arch
DESC: Architecture-as-code CLI — validate, query, and maintain architecture .arch files for any codebase

GUIDE:
arch is a single-binary CLI tool. All domain types live in schema.rs.
Shared loading and scanning infrastructure lives in context.rs (ArchContext).
Each command is a standalone module under src/commands/ — commands share code
through ArchContext (file walking) and extracted check() functions.
The stale command composes validate + coverage.
The scanner detects project type by file presence, not content parsing.
Before adding a command, check if an existing one already covers the use case.
ENDGUIDE

CONT: cli
CONT: schema
CONT: context
CONT: scanner
CONT: imports
CONT: resolve
CONT: depgraph
CONT: arch_parser
CONT: llmcode
CONT: lmindex
CONT: commands

RULE: schema-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: schema
  TO: commands; scanner; cli; context
  WHY: Schema types are pure data — no logic dependencies

RULE: scanner-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: scanner
  TO: commands; cli; context
  WHY: Scanner is a leaf utility — only used by init command

RULE: imports-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: imports
  TO: commands; scanner; cli; resolve; context
  WHY: Import extraction is a pure leaf utility — no logic dependencies

RULE: resolve-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: resolve
  TO: commands; scanner; cli; imports; context
  WHY: Resolution is a shared utility — depends only on schema types

RULE: context-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: context
  TO: commands; scanner; cli; imports
  WHY: Context is a shared loader — depends only on schema and resolve

RULE: init-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/init
  TO: commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/spec; commands/index
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: validate-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/validate
  TO: commands/init; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/spec; commands/index
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: coverage-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/coverage
  TO: commands/init; commands/validate; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/spec; commands/index
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: owns-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/owns
  TO: commands/init; commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/spec; commands/index
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: drift-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/drift
  TO: commands/init; commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/spec; commands/index
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: context-command-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/contextcmd
  TO: commands/init; commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/rename; commands/spec; commands/index; commands/stale
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: rename-command-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/rename
  TO: commands/init; commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/spec; commands/index; commands/stale
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: spec-command-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/spec
  TO: commands/init; commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/index; commands/stale
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: llmcode-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: llmcode
  TO: commands; context; imports; depgraph; resolve; lmindex
  WHY: llmcode is a pure leaf utility — depends only on schema, mirrors imports.rs position in the layer model

RULE: lmindex-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: lmindex
  TO: commands
  WHY: lmindex is a shared analysis layer — must not depend on commands to remain independently consumable

RULE: index-command-isolation
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: commands/index
  TO: commands/validate; commands/coverage; commands/owns; commands/drift; commands/fitness; commands/stories; commands/rules; commands/mermaid; commands/init; commands/stale; commands/contextcmd; commands/rename; commands/spec
  WHY: Leaf commands do not import other commands — each is independently testable

RULE: arch-parser-independence
  TYPE: no_dependency
  FROM: arch_parser
  TO: commands; cli; context; imports; depgraph; resolve; lmindex; llmcode; scanner
  WHY: arch_parser is a pure leaf — depends only on schema; no context loader, no command logic

RULE: arch-parser-callers
  TYPE: restrict_callers_to
  MODULE: arch_parser
  ALLOWED: context/context
  WHY: Only context may call arch_parser — arch source loading is exclusively context.rs's responsibility

STORY: user-runs-init
  DESC: User scaffolds architecture for a new project
  FLOW: cli/cli; scanner/scanner; commands/init

STORY: user-validates
  DESC: User checks architecture integrity after edits
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/validate

STORY: user-queries-ownership
  DESC: User finds which module owns a concept before editing
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/owns

STORY: user-checks-coverage
  DESC: User finds unmapped source files
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/coverage

STORY: user-checks-staleness
  DESC: User checks overall architecture health (validate + coverage combined)
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/stale

STORY: user-checks-drift
  DESC: User detects undeclared or forbidden dependencies by scanning source imports
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/drift

STORY: user-checks-fitness
  DESC: User validates architectural rules against actual code
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/fitness

STORY: user-checks-stories
  DESC: User verifies that story flows are backed by real import connections
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/stories

STORY: user-generates-diagrams
  DESC: User generates Mermaid architecture diagrams for documentation
  FLOW: cli/cli; commands/mermaid

STORY: user-deep-init
  DESC: User scaffolds architecture with inferred modules from project files
  FLOW: cli/cli; scanner/scanner; commands/init











